The repository contains source code. The generated release distributes an
independently built phonemizer, its corresponding source and patch/build recipe,
a pinned ONNX runtime, model configuration and Thorsten voice model. It is
separate from the MIT application. The root MIT license does not relicense these
components. Human Wikimedia recordings are not bundled or cached here.

Phonemizer source:
https://github.com/rhasspy/espeak-ng/tree/0f65aa301e0d6bae5e172cc74197d32a6182200f
https://github.com/wide-video/piper-phonemize/tree/cfff8e52ebaea37c7e953ae2d06b174acb827ac4
The eSpeak library is GPL-3.0-or-later with bundled data notices. Piper's wrapper
has its own MIT notice, retained in the source archive and generated notices.
The compatibility patch includes wchar.h before the ucd character macros when
compiling for Emscripten. German and English dictionaries are retained in the
runtime data package; unused dictionaries are omitted. The complete pinned
sources, modifications and build recipe are supplied as source.tar.gz.

Build tools:
Emscripten 3.1.47, via emsdk commit
708dcbcc9ee23bc7d2dad44fc90db377e38b771c.
https://github.com/emscripten-core/emsdk
Emscripten, libc, libc++, libc++abi, libunwind and compiler runtime notices are
retained in generated NOTICES.txt. Compiler tools are not bundled in the app.
The build is from pinned source; byte-identical builds across host toolchains
are not claimed.

ONNX Runtime Web 1.18.0:
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/tree/v1.18.0
MIT; its license and full third-party notice file accompany the release.
The runtime executes in one worker thread without a remote speech service.

Voice:
Thorsten Mueller / https://github.com/thorstenMueller/Thorsten-Voice
Model mirrored at the fixed revision:
https://huggingface.co/diffusionstudio/piper-voices/tree/840e38a7e26d813bd6221b78cfbaefa3585b3f71/de/de_DE/thorsten/medium
The supplied MODEL_CARD describes CC0 Thorsten data and fine-tuning from the
Lessac medium voice. Preserve that card alongside the model repository terms;
recording data, model weights and program code have separate provenance.
Output is synthesized speech, not a human recording. Pronunciation quality is
not guaranteed for every imported name, abbreviation, phrase or homograph.

Source access:
The release offers source.tar.gz and rebuild.sh at the same versioned download
location as its runtime. They are available separately through Source code;
installation does not fetch an unused source archive onto a learner's device.
Generated NOTICES.txt includes the complete applicable upstream license texts.

The early VITS Web / diffusionstudio piper-wasm prototype is not redistributed.
This release uses the separately compiled pinned-source phonemizer instead.
